<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for Shadow Priest DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic for Phase 4. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from Heroics, reputation rewards, and the new 10-man &amp; 25-man Raid loot added to Titan Rune Dungeons.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot-gear">Shadow Priest DPS Best in Slot Gear, Gems, and Enchants - Pre-Raid Phase 4</h2>As a Shadow Priest your Hit cap is 17% for raid bosses. 3% is covered by the talent <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33193/misery">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_misery.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Misery</span></a> and 3% is covered by <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=15328/shadow-focus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_burningspirit.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shadow Focus</span></a>. This leaves you with 11% to cover in other ways. Alliance Priests with a <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span>Draenei in their party will have <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a>, giving them another 1%, cutting it down to 10%. This last 10/<wbr/>11% is gotten from gear, but it is not going to make or break your character in a lot of situations, and sacrificing too much to get to your Hit cap can be a DPS loss. Outside of Hit, you have no other "caps". There is no Haste cap or break point to worry about as a Shadow Priest. <br/>
<br/>Ideally you will want to spend your <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> on Tier 10 items such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50392/crimson-acolyte-cowl">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_156.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crimson Acolyte Cowl</span></a> to build your <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-250/sanctified-crimson-acolytes-regalia">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctified Crimson Acolyte's Regalia</span></a> as soon as possible. Unfortunately, gathering enough without entering Icecrown Citadel is going to be a slow and unnecessary process. As such, this list does not include <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> items. <br/>
<br/>This set does consist mostly of items bought with <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=2589/sidereal-essence">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_icediamond_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sidereal Essence</span></span></a> and <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=2711/defilers-scourgestone">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Defiler's Scourgestone</span></span></a>. While it is unlikely that you will farm every piece, the road there could lead to hundreds of combinations of loot, making it very difficult to predict what slots you end up behind in. Spend your currencies appropriately, upgrading the slots most in need first. A lot of the items listed have equivalent items with or without Hit also, allowing you to pick and mix as needed.<br/>
<br/>
